# Module names in this file will be included in the cam magiclantern.zip
bench
dual_iso
file_man
mlv_lite
# mlv_play: in-camera MLV review.  Enable BOTH mlv_play and silent in the
# Modules menu - mlv_play's only unresolved symbol is lossless_decompress_raw,
# which silent exports, and cross-module symbols resolve only if both modules
# are actually loaded.
#
# silent is a dependency here, not a feature: leave "Silent Picture" switched
# OFF.  Its silent_pic_polling_cbr() returns on the first line when the feature
# is disabled, and its raw_lv_request() calls only run while a silent picture is
# actually being taken, so a loaded-but-disabled silent costs one comparison per
# shoot-task tick and nothing else.  (It was briefly suspected of causing the
# second-take recording failure; that turned out to be the buffer realloc bug in
# mlv_lite - see DEVLOG.)
#
# Our MLVs are uncompressed - lossless encoding is DIGIC 5 only - so the
# decompressor is never actually called.  Playback of 1920-wide 14-bit is slow;
# it is for checking a take, not reviewing at speed.
mlv_play
silent
# adtglog2: hooks CMOS_write (0xe053cdc4) and logs every register list Canon
# sends to the sensor, with the caller's LR, to adtg.log in the card root.
# Research tool for video dual ISO (which LiveView ISO table is live) and for
# crop modes (which list each readout mode sends).  Enable in Modules only
# for a logging session; it costs a little CPU on every CMOS write.
adtglog2
# d7probe: read-only research probe (Debug > D7 probe dump) - hooks the LV
# prepro path update and SetSDClkFrequency to log bit-depth / SD clock params.
# Loads only if ML/SETTINGS/d7probe.en exists.
d7probe
